.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; up-vbcc install: the vbcc C compiler for AmigaOS 68k (vc, vbccm68k, vasm, vlink, the m68k-amigaos
; target) in UP-Term:vbcc, with the VBCC: assign, its path and the VBCC environment variable
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, stops the install when up-term.lha is
; missing or too old (the reason is in ENV:UPTCHECK).
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab copy-vbcc
; The drawer userland/vbcc (the author's archives, unmodified, plus UP-Term's config/upterm68k) goes to
; UP-Term:vbcc, the path config/upterm68k and startup.txt name. userland holds what dist/slim.txt names;
; Copy of a drawer copies what is in it.
MakeDir >NIL: UP-Term:licenses
Copy userland UP-Term: ALL CLONE QUIET
If WARN
  Quit 20
EndIf
; VBCC: assigned now and at every boot: a block in S:User-Startup that assigns only while UP-Term:vbcc
; is there, so one left behind by an Uninstall that could not take it out does no harm. The Amiga NDK
; headers are not part of this package: NDKINC: stays the owner's assign (README.txt).
Assign VBCC: UP-Term:vbcc
Path VBCC:bin ADD
SetEnv VBCC VBCC:
Search >NIL: S:User-Startup ";BEGIN vbcc"
If WARN
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";BEGIN vbcc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "If EXISTS UP-Term:vbcc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  Assign VBCC: UP-Term:vbcc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  Path VBCC:bin ADD"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  SetEnv VBCC VBCC:"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "EndIf"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";END vbcc"
  If WARN
    Quit 20
  EndIf
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "VBCC installed: in an UP-Term window  vc +upterm68k hello.c -o hello  (NDKINC: needs the NDK headers, see README.txt)."
